  "id": "bradycardia",
  "term": "bradycardia",
  "definition": "Bradycardia, specifically sinus bradycardia, means a resting heart rhythm from the sinus node that is slower than 60 beats per minute. It can occur as a normal finding, such as during sleep or in athletic people, or as a sign of illness; while it often does not need intervention, persistent severe slowing can be dangerous.",
